+# v0.5.0 candidate provenance and scope
+
+Prepared 28 October 2026. This guide is new release material; it does not
+revise the original mathematical proof, outputs, audit or corrections.
+
+**Identity.** The repository HEAD at consolidation is
+`2c337bb4a52a7e79430c6430413893dd79c6e9e4`. The alpha theorem, October 27
+corrections and October 28 audit existed as uncommitted/untracked working
+files. HEAD alone is not their source identity. The candidate manifest
+records exact per-file bytes and origins, plus that distinction. No commit,
+Git tag, branch rewrite or release is created by the packaging procedure.
+
+**Four kinds of material.**
+
+| Role | Treatment |
+|---|---|
+| Original alpha proof, scripts, reports, figures and exploratory records | Copied byte for byte at their original relative paths; frozen as references, including unsuccessful exploratory trials with their real status |
+| Earlier baseline, reviews, corrections, and October 28 audit | Preserved bytes; the published v0.4.0 archive remains separate from its private research freeze |
+| New release contents | This guide, the candidate README, `V050_CLAIMS.json`, the manifest, safe reproduction and integrity tests; explicitly attributed to this consolidation |
+| Regenerated outputs | Created only in a new external run directory; not written over original reports and not smuggled into the original provenance |
+
+The file inventory gives the role and source hash of every member. Original
+workspace files are checked against the October 28 audit's pre-existing
+`original_hashes.json` where applicable, plus the original aggregate's source
+and report bindings. A separate workspace before/after check preserves all
+pre-existing tracked material and the relevant untracked research/audit trees.
+That workspace record is a preparation receipt, not a Git commit identity.
+
+The published archive has SHA-256
+`20328551989ac1fe7ff7bd5d5b6c28a9eac52bf5d7b8dcbd11b3ac92866481f9`.
+Its identity comes from the preserved v0.4.0 publication receipt. Its public
+source manifest covers 78 files; the unchanged private scientific freeze
+covers 37 files. These counts refer to different recorded packages. The new
+candidate does not rewrite either manifest or make them interchangeable.
+
+**No silent scientific variants.** The active alpha algorithms and their
+four imported audit/kernel dependencies retain their original bytes. The
+new runner invokes their existing `--report` options; `audit_cover` also gets
+the new `--input`. The unsafe historical aggregate is retained for provenance
+and is not executed by the new entry point. No model, polynomial, interval,
+trajectory, certificate, sign algorithm, threshold or theorem is patched.
+
+The only corrected output field is the top-level `/scope` in a newly
+consolidated `exact_results.json`. Its old value falsely attributes universal
+inner inclusion to v0.4.0. The original file and newly generated raw file keep
+that old field verbatim. A separate correction record identifies the precise
+old and new strings. Every consolidated report receives a checked
+`proof_scope` from the new frozen ledger. Removing those additions and
+restoring the old scope must reproduce the raw report exactly.
+
+**Proof responsibilities.**
+
+| Stage | Responsibility | Does not establish alone |
+|---|---|---|
+| `verify_phase` | Low-dimensional fixed-K results, exact boundary polynomials and global exclusions | New universal inner inclusion |
+| `audit_phase` | Formal moment identities, prefix constants, finite vector/integer cross-checks | Arbitrary K/time positivity by sampling |
+| `finite_cover` | Continuous-alpha, all-time finite complement through K=203 and K=10 upper continuation | Uniform K>=204 |
+| `audit_cover` | Reconstruct finite coverage with a second exact sign algorithm and rejection controls | Fully independent model/trajectory implementation |
+| `uniform_probe` | Continuous parameter boxes covering all K>=204 and the all-time loss comparison | Global outside-interval exclusions |
+| New aggregate | Check agreement and assemble these already-audited obligations | A new independent theorem proof |
+| Published v0.4.0 replay | Reproduce its original narrow-interval result | The wider B inclusion |
+| October 28 audit-program replay | Reproduce its independent kernel/interpolation/witness calculations | A new independent audit of the entire box proof |
+
+Theorem A's invariants, non-stopping and boundary residence remain analytic
+dependencies. The Bernstein and Sturm passes share model/trajectory algebra.
+The formal bin-sum check and interval proof share some formulas. These are
+useful distinct checks, not proof-assistant verification or human peer review.
+
+**Freeze and reproduction.** The manifest is written after preparation,
+before isolated mathematical execution. It enumerates every actual package
+file except itself, with SHA-256, size, role and origin. A detached receipt
+pins its digest and the deterministic ZIP digest. Hashes generated after a
+run cannot replace the preflight inventory or validate evidence that was
+overwritten before the check.
+
+Reproduction first checks the exact package file list, file hashes,
+historical report/source bindings, stage scope ledger and audited payload
+digests. It then creates a new external output directory. The package is
+checked again after all stages, including the old evidence. Timing and the
+dependent finite-witness runtime hash are the only semantic comparison
+exceptions; both old and new witness bindings are separately verified.
+Any discrepancy in scientific content fails the run.
